anded on Vancouver Island]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133035427.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/indian-origin-hiker-found-alive-after-3-nights-stranded-on-vancouver-island/articleshow/133035427.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/indian-origin-hiker-found-alive-after-3-nights-stranded-on-vancouver-island/articleshow/133035427.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-07T22:31:57+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Gokul Ankari</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133038945,imgsize-776980.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Harvard rejected Paul Devlin in 1981; he wrote back rejecting the rejection letter]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133034384.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In 1981, high school student Paul Devlin responded to Harvard University's rejection letter by rejecting its rejection instead. Inspired by a grammatical error in Harvard's letter, his witty reply was published byThe New York Times. More than four decades later, the letter has resurfaced online and continues to entertain readers.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/education/news/in-1981-harvard-rejected-paul-devlin-he-spotted-a-grammatical-error-rejected-the-rejection-and-had-his-response-published-in-the-new-york-times/articleshow/133034384.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/education/news/in-1981-harvard-rejected-paul-devlin-he-spotted-a-grammatical-error-rejected-the-rejection-and-had-his-response-published-in-the-new-york-times/articleshow/133034384.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-07T19:00:00+05:30</pubDate><enc